# How Do I Grow Berries and Soft Fruit in My Garden?

## Short Answer

Growing berries and soft fruit is one of the most rewarding additions to any garden or permaculture system.
Soft fruits include strawberries, raspberries, blackberries, blueberries, currants, gooseberries, elderberries, and lesser-known options like haskap and goji berries.
Most berry bushes are perennial, meaning you plant them once and harvest for years with proper care.
The keys to success are choosing the right varieties for your climate, preparing soil with adequate organic matter, and understanding each plant's pruning and feeding needs.

## Detailed Explanation

### Choosing the Right Berry Types

Your first decision is which berries suit your space, climate, and taste preferences.
